  "episode": 14,
  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "title": "Say It to My Face",
  "dates": "Wednesday, November 4 – Sunday, November 8, 2009",
  "logline": "Becca has a question, Professor Hale throws a dinner party at the edge of a cliff, and for one long Saturday Jack is exactly the friend Lena needs.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "On All Souls, Wes ended it on the phone. Lena, on the stairs: he said she’d marry him anyway, so he couldn’t let her.",
      "if": "lena_wes_over"
    },
    {
      "text": "At dawn on the stairs you decided to wait. She wants to be asked — and you don’t ask anybody the night her house falls down.",
      "if": "e13_reason==\"asked\""
    },
    {
      "text": "“Jack. What are you going to do?” “Whatever you need.” “I know. You always do.”",
      "if": "e13_dawn==\"need\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Theo’s mother asked how long you and Lena had been together. “We’re not — Becca’s with me.” Becca: “He’s *mine*!” Lena: “Nobody’s, as of last night.”",
      "if": "e13_caroline==\"becca\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Your first night, Lena read the back of your postcard twice and asked who A.H. was, like she didn’t care.",
      "if": "e1_postcard_seen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Becca, at 12:49 a.m.: “Can we talk tomorrow? Nothing bad!! Good thing. :)”"
    }
  ],
